<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/037E">Corollary <span data-tag="037E">5.3.4.22</span>.</a> Let $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}$ be a functor which carries each morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ to an isomorphism of simplicial sets. Then the morphism $\lambda _{t}:  \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}( \mathscr {F} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\mathscr {F}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ of Remark <a data-tag="0374" href="/tag/0374">5.3.4.12</a> is an isomorphism. </p>
